      "output_text": "### Side camera\n- The robot arm and gripper are visible beside the open instrument. The fingers and light-colored cuvette overlap the instrument’s front edge; their lower portions are partly occluded.\n- The white source rack is visible on the table in front of the instrument, but individual slot identities, including **A1**, are not readable.\n- The instrument lid is raised, exposing a dark, elongated opening. Some interior detail is visible near the hinge, but the internal seats are not clearly resolved. The designated **candidate_far_hinge** seat cannot be reliably identified.\n\n### Wrist camera\n- The gripper is shown close-up, with two black finger pads flanking a pale, upright rectangular cuvette. Its open top and much of its long body are clearly visible; the pads obscure portions of its sides.\n- The white rack and its grid of square openings are clearly visible behind and to the right of the cuvette. No slot labels are legible, and the cuvette’s relationship to slot A1 cannot be established.\n- The instrument housing occupies the left side, but its loading opening and internal seat are outside the useful view or occluded.\n\n**Visibility assessment:** The wrist view provides the clearest evidence of the cuvette between the fingers; the side view provides the instrument-opening context. Neither image provides sufficient detail to verify target-seat alignment, insertion depth, seat support, release, or a completed transfer.",
